# LOCAL run (2026-11-08, user: "lets fix this with reward scale", then "1) remove value
# clips 2) remove actor normalization - i want implementation to plain SAC 3) multiply
# reward in environment"): the local Town05 standard-SAC fine-tune from c0
# (slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac.env: encoder + GRU frozen, c0's demos pinned with the
# arrival approach cut, learned log-std, auto-tuned temperature starting at c0's
# stored 0.1) with:
#   * REWARD_SCALE=10 IN THE ENVIRONMENT (torch_rl.reward_scale.ScaledReward on the env;
#     HER's relabelled rows and the preloaded demos get the same x10 where they enter
#     the replay; the learner scales nothing).
#   * NO value clips on the critic target (plain SAC has none).
#   * ACTOR_Q_NORM=0: the actor loss is plain SAC's alpha * log pi - Q (the v13
#     Q / std(Q) normalisation also cancelled any reward scale).
# Why the scale: rewards are ~0.27/step, and widening c0's actor from its precision
# (-log pi ~ -2.7) to near-uniform (+1.35) is worth alpha x ~4 nats per step: +0.41 at
# alpha 0.1, more than the driving reward -- c0's noise went near-uniform within ~80
# updates and its driving collapsed (training success .82 -> .03). At x10 the driving
# reward is ~2.7/step and that gain ~15% of it.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_c0ft_t05_sac.env"
export REWARD_SCALE=10 ACTOR_Q_NORM=0
export TQC_VALUE_FLOOR=none TQC_VALUE_CEILING=none
export EXPLORE_VALUE_FLOOR=none EXPLORE_VALUE_CEILING=none
